            <ArticleTitle>[Mystery diagnosis: &quot;the Rolling Stones' syndrome&quot;].</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">gin/31.5.14</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present an unusual case of a young patient regularly followed in our Chronic Renal Insufficiency ambulatory with the periodicity of 2-3 visits per year--with stabilization of his residual renal function. The patient came to the emergency department declaring abdominal pain but make a diagnosis turned out to be more complicated than we expected.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
